===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|tanglen}}, probably of {{der|en|gmq|}} origin, compare {{cog|sv|taggla|t=to disorder}}, {{cog|non|þǫngull}}, {{m|non|þang|t=tangle; seaweed}}, see Etymology 2 below.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[mix]] [[together]] or [[intertwine]].
#: {{syn|en|entangle|knot|mat|snarl|Thesaurus:tangle}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become [[mixed]] [[together]] or [[intertwined]].
#: {{syn|en|dishevel|tousle}}
#: {{ant|en|untangle|unsnarl}}
#: {{ux|en|Her hair was '''tangled''' from a day in the wind.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figurative}} To [[enter into]] an [[argument]], [[conflict]], [[dispute]], or [[fight]].
#: {{syn|en|argue|conflict|dispute|fight}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't '''tangle''' with someone three times your size.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''tangled''' with the law.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Daisuke Wakabayashi|title=Who Gets the L.L.C.? Inside a Silicon Valley Billionaire’s Divorce.|date=2021-08-20|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/20/technology/Scott-Hassan-Allison-Huynh-divorce.html|passage=After a few attempts at counseling, they separated in January 2015. Since then, they have '''tangled''' in the courts.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251031200555/https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/20/technology/Scott-Hassan-Allison-Huynh-divorce.html|archivedate=31 October 2025}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[catch]] and [[hold]].
#: {{syn|en|ensnare|entrap}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|2|passage='''tangled''' in amorous nets}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1646|author=w:Richard Crashaw|title=Steps to the Temple
|passage=When my simple weakness strays, / '''Tangled''' in forbidden ways.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001| title=Tangled Up in Red, White, and Blue: New Social Movements in America| author=Christine A. Kelly| ISBN=0742508137 |passage=This is a book about the potential for the reclamation, reform, and enlightened transformation of the most expansive elements of the liberal tradition— that social and economic justice remain '''tangled''' in liberalism's web of pretentious institutions and betrayed promises is the reason for this battle from within.}}

